  "name": "Talk Box",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Talking formant bass: the Vowel table one octave above a clean sine sub, Mod A (triangle, 1/4, grid-locked) scanning the vowels and shifting the formants while Mod B on the same grid moves a BP12 band with them, light Saturate. Held notes keep talking; short notes catch one vowel. Play: held and tied notes around F1-C2, mono legato. Tweak: Mod A/Mod B Division for the talking speed, Mod A Index amount for the vowel range, Mod A Shift amount for formant size, Filter A Res for nasal bite. FX: Overdrive +6 dB with a Post low-pass at 6 kHz, multiband squash at 70 % (time 40 %) so the vowel formants jump out, an EQ low cut at 25 Hz and +2 dB presence at 1.2 kHz, Dimension (size 0.3, wet low cut 200 Hz) and a 7 % short plate. Each note starts on a slightly different vowel and harder hits brighten the band. Macros: Talk deepens the vowel scan, Vowel moves the formants and the band, Nasal sharpens the band and Dirt adds grit.",
